Rem ==================================================================
Rem emley-moor.shoddy — the shell: a port, a greeting, and the loop.
Rem
Rem     mill run --allow-net mills/emley-moor/emley-moor.shoddy
Rem     (then open http://127.0.0.1:8080/ in a browser)
Rem
Rem Everything that decides anything is in emley-moor-core.shoddy, and
Rem the part of it worth arguing about is one pure function:
Rem
Rem     Respond(request As String) As String
Rem
Rem Raw request text in, raw response text out — no socket, no clock, no
Rem state. That is why test.shoddy can grade every route by calling it
Rem with a string, with no network and no --allow-net. This file is the
Rem twenty lines that could not be pure: accept, read, write, close.
Rem
Rem The split is mungo-caverns' — a turn is a function there, a request
Rem is a function here — and it is the reason a web server in this
Rem repository has assertions rather than a screenshot.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "net.shoddy"
Include "emley-moor-core.shoddy"

Def Main()
    Let srv = Listen(port)
    Print("emley-moor listening on http://127.0.0.1:" & Str(port) & "/")
    Print("Ctrl-C to stop.")
    ServeForever(srv)
